  "finalText": [
    "No. Docker stop at t=1320 does not bind Node.\n\nCounterexample: Node starts at t=1000 with a 1206s relative limit, so it may run until t=2206. The timer kills Docker only, so Node keeps working past the t=1350 all-work deadline.\n\nSmallest correction: cap Node by remaining wall time, `min(1206, 1350 \u2212 start)` (here 350s), or make the independent timer kill all work, not Docker only.",
    "No. Docker stop at t=1320 does not bind Node.\n\nCounterexample: Node starts at t=1000 with a 1206s relative limit, so it may run until t=2206. The timer kills Docker only, so Node keeps working past the t=1350 all-work deadline.\n\nSmallest correction: cap Node by remaining wall time, `min(1206, 1350 \u2212 start)` (here 350s), or make the independent timer kill all work, not Docker only."
